{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310861,"nonce":"hbKeymGC8s/N9YMW5BD5n1wZF4I=","title":"SDOT direct-dot for Q4_K_M @ Q8_K matmul. The +25% perf win shipped earlier as dot_q4_k_q8 + lazy x_q8_cache. Commit 327fd80 adds ...","message":"SDOT direct-dot Q4_K_M @ Q8_K matmul history and current state.\n\n**Key honest finding from workflow wzbim2n5l**: The actual SDOT inner kernel (`dot_q4_k_q8` + lazy `x_q8_cache` in `qmatmul_chunk_impl`) was **already shipping default-ON** as of an earlier Q4_K_M bring-up commit, delivering the +25% win (0.66 → 0.82 tok/s). Per `project_quant_haxe_wip.md`'s \"Phase 4 INT8+Q4_K_M e2e working\" — that win was already in the baseline. The workflow's audit caught this before designing redundant work.\n\nCommit `327fd80` ships what's actually new: spec-shaped public API surface + per-call shim strip + portability hardening + honest framing of the multi-prompt divergence.\n\n\n**Spec-shaped API**: `Q8KBlock` (292 B, repr(C)) and `Q4KMBlock` (144 B, repr(C, packed(1))) match `ggml-quants.h` byte-for-byte (compile-time asserted at `quant.rs:847-850`). `quantize_row_q8_K` + `vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K` match llama.cpp's symbol names.\n\n**Shim strip**: New `dot_q4_k_q8_kblock` reads `Q8KBlock` directly via `vld1q_s8` off `Q8KBlock.qs` and folds the per-32-elem sum inline as `bsums[4p]+bsums[4p+1]` / `bsums[4p+2]+bsums[4p+3]` widened to i32 where it multiplies into `sum_term2`. Replaces the prior 256-byte memcpy + `bsums_16` fill + 8-entry pair-sum loop in `vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K` that ran ~65k times per FFN matmul (~16 MB pure memcpy per matmul). Legacy `dot_q4_k_q8(*const u8, \u0026Q8Block)` stays for `qmatmul_chunk_impl`'s `x_q8_cache` path.\n\n**Portability gates** (three-layer):\n1. Compile-time: `cfg(all(target_arch=\"aarch64\", target_feature=\"dotprod\"))` decides linkage; `#[target_feature(enable=\"dotprod\")]` on inner kernels.\n2. Runtime: `sdot_enabled()` lazily probes `is_aarch64_feature_detected!(\"dotprod\")` into a `OnceLock\u003cbool\u003e` so +dotprod-built binaries running on pre-ARMv8.2 cores (Cortex-A53/A55r0/A57/A72/A73) fall back to scalar instead of SIGILLing.\n3. Env: `RAYZOR_USE_SDOT=0` force-off override preserved.\n\nScalar dequant-then-dot reference arm at `vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K` is now always-reachable, serving runtime-probe-fail AND non-aarch64 builds uniformly.\n\n\n| Metric | SDOT-OFF | SDOT-ON | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wall (s) | 15.266 ± 0.572 | 15.298 ± 0.358 | +0.21% (t=0.11, zero) |\n| tok/s | 0.802 | 0.801 | -0.1% |\n| User CPU (s) | 16.894 | 16.470 | **-2.5% on every run (5/5)** |\n\n**Per-op kernel IS leaner** (consistent user-CPU drop). **Wall-clock savings are masked** by memory bandwidth on weight fetches + per-token harness overhead at 0.8 tok/s. Expected to compound once worker pool actually loads (currently ~1.1 CPU/wall = effectively single-threaded — see [[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]]).\n\n\n- llama.cpp Metal: 135.81 tok/s\n- llama.cpp CPU (5-6 cores): 72.40 tok/s\n- Rayzor today: 0.8 tok/s\n- Gap: ~88× vs llama.cpp CPU, ~165× vs Metal\n\nPer the workflow synthesis: at CPU/wall ~1.1, the dominant remaining bottleneck is **parallelism not compute density**. SDOT and addInto kernel wins can't translate to wall time when the 6-worker pool is effectively single-threaded.\n\n\n- compiler --lib: 709/709\n- rayzor-runtime --lib: 113/113 (incl. 3 new SDOT spec-shape tests)\n- haxe: 127/128 (pre-existing `test_exception` SIGTRAP flake per [[bugs-test-exception-flake]])\n- tiny-transformer: === PASS ===\n- llama-chat \"What is the capital of France?\" 12 → MATCH byte-for-byte vs llama.cpp under both `RAYZOR_USE_SDOT=0` and `=1`\n\n\n`tools/llama-diff/compare.sh` divergence on haiku and Hamlet prompts vs llama.cpp **reproduces on pre-SDOT HEAD** and is byte-identical under `RAYZOR_USE_SDOT=0` and `=1` on current HEAD. Root cause: harness sampler-config mismatch — compare.sh runs llama.cpp with `--temp 0` (true argmax) but rayzor with `temperature=0.01 → LocalTempSampler(0.01, rep_penalty=1.15, topK=50, seed=42)`. The 1.15 repetition penalty is a structural argmax shift: Paris matches because top-1 dominates by \u003e log(1.15); haiku/Hamlet have smaller top-1/top-2 gaps where the penalty flips argmax. See [[bugs-sdot-multi-prompt-validation-gap]].\n\n\n1. **[[bugs-pool-data-flow-gap]]** — workers ~1.1 CPU/wall = single-threaded; closing parallelism amplifies SDOT (+addInto, +pool) into actual throughput gains. Highest ROI by a wide margin.\n2. **[[bugs-addinto-rebind-clone-drop-failure]]** — LlamaModel.hx:65 clone-drop unlocks ~3 MB allocator churn / 24-token decode.\n3. **SMMLA for M2+** (FEAT_I8MM, 8× density over SDOT — not available on M1).\n4. **F32 SVE / i8mm path** where available.\n\n\n- `wzbim2n5l` — initial SDOT workflow (8 agents). Returned yellow with the honest finding that SDOT was already shipping. Three must-fix items.\n- `wz8f59bw8` — remediation (5 agents). Stripped shim, tightened portability, root-caused multi-prompt divergence as pre-existing sampler-config. All must-fixes resolved. Single commit `327fd80` shipped green.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_sdot_qmatmul` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}